<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Smim Htaw</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1740">1740</a>–<a href="/years/1747">1747</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Smim Htaw was the king chosen at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bago">Pegu</a> in 1740 by the Mon and other rebels of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burma">Lower Burma</a> who rose against the Toungoo dynasty of Ava, reviving the name of the Hanthawaddy kingdom. A former monk, he proved a weak ruler and was replaced in 1747 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binnya-dala">Binnya Dala</a>, who went on to capture Ava in 1752.</p></div>
